Karkov, whom the Weft call Kharkov, is a human [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Duskwalker|Duskwalker]] in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]]. He is an older man with blue skin, and he wears the deep blue uniform of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. Legions of people who agree with him follow him. He has taken all three of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] bloods at once, which makes him more powerful.

He stands high in the First House and once kept two lieutenants close: the elven woman called [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|the Slipseer]] and the orc [[People/Althane/Rampart|Rampart]], who is now dead and was her brother. He has a strong interest in finding the Weft, who made themselves known to him once when they were weak and then vanished from his sight. He holds one of the few ultraviolet keycards to [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and during the crisis there he is on its sixth floor, in the Eschatology division, seeing to doomsday preparations while the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] tries to reach his mind and drag him down into slumber. He means to fight it.

The Weft knew Karkov as a coworker, and hold that he does what he believes is best for everyone. They also hold that he is the champion of [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]], whether he knows it or not. [[People/Althane/Masha|Masha]] says that if he is ever made to run, it will be to the bottom floor of the House's complex, where a passage leads off; she knows the passage only from its far end.
